DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ggeettllooaaddaavvgg() function returns the number of processes in the system
       run  queue  averaged over various periods of time.  Up to _n samples are
       retrieved and assigned to successive elements of _l_o_a_d_a_v_g_[_].  The system
       imposes a maximum of 3 samples, representing averages over the last  1,
       5, and 15 minutes, respectively.

